# Build the Android app

Run from `flutter/`. Use `required_permissions: ["all"]`.

## APK for the phone

```bash
# Might take a couple of minutes
flutter build apk --release
```

Output location: `build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk`

Copy it to Downloads so it's easy to send to the phone:

```bash
rm -f ~/Downloads/app-release.apk && cp build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk ~/Downloads/app-release.apk
```

The release build is signed with the debug key. That is fine for installing by hand, not for the Play Store.

## Run on the emulator

```bash
flutter emulators                          # list: Pixel_8_API_35, Medium_Phone_API_35
flutter emulators --launch Pixel_8_API_35  # opens the emulator window
flutter run                                # once it has booted; -d emulator-5554 if more than one device
```

In the `flutter run` terminal, `r` hot reloads, `R` restarts, `q` quits.

From an agent shell, `flutter emulators --launch` dies when the command ends. Start the emulator as a background task instead:

```bash
~/Library/Android/sdk/emulator/emulator -avd Pixel_8_API_35 -no-snapshot-save -no-audio
```

`adb exec-out screencap` returns a black image on this emulator. Use `adb emu screenrecord screenshot /tmp/shot.png` (adb is `~/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools/adb`).
